# Story 26: Agent Output Routing (40s)
# Hook: Route agent output to any pane -- monitor your agents in real time.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-26-agent-output.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- we'll route agent output to a named pane.

[00:04.0 --> 00:06.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode.

[00:06.0 --> 00:10.0]
Create an agent that watches for issues.

[00:10.0 --> 00:14.0]
Name this pane so we can reference it.

[00:14.0 --> 00:18.0]
Route the monitor agent's output to my-pane. Everything the agent says will appear here.

[00:18.0 --> 00:30.0]
Ask the agent to check the current directory. Output streams to the registered pane.

[00:30.0 --> 00:34.0]
The agent's response appears in the named pane.

[00:34.0 --> 00:38.0]
Unregister when you no longer need the routing.

[00:38.0 --> 00:40.0]
Output routing: full control over where agent responses go.

